  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "106",
  "quote": "The amount of a rent deposit shall not be more than the lesser of the amount of rent for one rent period and the amount of rent for one month.",
  "reason": "Section 106(2) limits the maximum rent deposit to the amount of rent for one month or one rent period, whichever is lesser. Because the clause requires a deposit equal to two months' rent, it is inconsistent with the Act and is therefore void under section 4(1)."
}

